4414e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,82345,279,1985,1124,9697,59,26888,220,20,41715,26888,21,41715,26888,22,2376,30529,26888,220,20,41715,26888,21,41715,26888,22,2376,59,26888,220,20,30529,26888,21,41715,26888,22,2376,59,26888,220,20,41715,26888,21,30529,26888,22,72341,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nEvaluate the product \\[(\\sqrt 5+\\sqrt6+\\sqrt7)(-\\sqrt 5+\\sqrt6+\\sqrt7)(\\sqrt 5-\\sqrt6+\\sqrt7)(\\sqrt 5+\\sqrt6-\\sqrt7).\\]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"240045541b2fddda62a12db78181306ce3644a8bff4d96c2e19fcc74ebf36670"},"seconds":47.985862016677856,"seed":443631692926277682,"stop":"eos","text":"To evaluate the product \\[(\\sqrt 5+\\sqrt6+\\sqrt7)(-\\sqrt 5+\\sqrt6+\\sqrt7)(\\sqrt 5-\\sqrt6+\\sqrt7)(\\sqrt 5+\\sqrt6-\\sqrt7),\\] let's denote \\(a = \\sqrt{5}\\), \\(b = \\sqrt{6}\\), and \\(c = \\sqrt{7}\\). Then the expression becomes \\((a+b+c)(-a+b+c)(a-b+c)(a+b-c)\\).\n\nWe can use the identity for the product of differences and sums of roots, which is similar to the identity for the difference of squares but applied to four terms. Specifically, we can use the identity:\n\n\\[\n(x+y+z)(-x+y+z)(x-y+z)(x+y-z) = (x^2 + y^2 + z^2 - 2xy - 2xz - 2yz)(x^2 + y^2 + z^2 + 2xy + 2xz + 2yz)\n\\]\n\nHowever, a simpler approach is to recognize that the expression can be rewritten using the identity for the product of the sums and differences of three terms. We can group the terms as follows:\n\n\\[\n((b+c)^2 - a^2)((a^2 - (b-c)^2))\n\\]\n\nFirst, let's simplify each part:\n\n1. \\((b+c)^2 - a^2 = (b+c-a)(b+c+a)\\)\n2. \\((a^2 - (b-c)^2) = (a - (b-c))(a + (b-c)) = (a - b + c)(a + b - c)\\)\n\nSo the original expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n((b+c)^2 - a^2)((a^2 - (b-c)^2)) = ((b+c)^2 - a^2)(a^2 - (b-c)^2)\n\\]\n\nNow we substitute back \\(a = \\sqrt{5}\\), \\(b = \\sqrt{6}\\), and \\(c = \\sqrt{7}\\):\n\n\\[\n((\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{7})^2 - (\\sqrt{5})^2)((\\sqrt{5})^2 - (\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{7})^2)\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term separately:\n\n\\[\n(\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{7})^2 = 6 + 7 + 2\\sqrt{42} = 13 + 2\\sqrt{42}\n\\]\n\\[\n(\\sqrt{5})^2 = 5\n\\]\n\\[\n(\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{7})^2 = 6 + 7 - 2\\sqrt{42} = 13 - 2\\sqrt{42}\n\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n(13 + 2\\sqrt{42} - 5)(5 - (13 - 2\\sqrt{42})) = (8 + 2\\sqrt{42})(5 - 13 + 2\\sqrt{42}) = (8 + 2\\sqrt{42})(-8 + 2\\sqrt{42})\n\\]\n\nThis is a difference of squares:\n\n\\[\n(8 + 2\\sqrt{42})(-8 + 2\\sqrt{42}) = (2\\sqrt{42})^2 - 8^2 = 4 \\cdot 42 - 64 = 168 - 64 = 104\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of the product is \\(\\boxed{104}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{104}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
